//
// SmolVLA compile-only smoke test: builds every SigLIP vision ELF through the
// AIR -> AIE -> aiecc -> Peano pipeline. No NPU dispatch, no HuggingFace
// download, no lerobot import — so it runs anywhere the toolchain is installed.
//
// Covers the two fused multi-launch ELFs (vit_ln_qkv, vit_o_ffn), the
// single-launch registry flash_attn, the post-LayerNorm and the connector
// projection.
//
// CI collects this through `check-programming-examples-llms-compile`, whose
// filter is the path `llms/.*/run_npu2_compile` — no filename suffix needed.
// That target runs only when HF_TOKEN is available (pushes to main /
// workflow_dispatch); the per-PR gate is llama32_1b's compile lit alone.
//
// Needs no lerobot: the entry point imports torch and lerobot lazily, so this
// runs with only the mlir-air toolchain plus llama32_1b's requirements.txt,
// which is what CI installs.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_compile
// RUN: cd test_peano_compile
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: Compilation passed.
